
  var EVAL_HTML = "\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Heuristic evaluation of the current checkout</h2>\n    <p>\n      <b>26 findings</b>, evaluated against <b>Nielsen's ten usability heuristics</b>. Evidence is the recorded walkthrough of\n      <b>qa.highbasemarket.com</b> \u2014 cart \u2192 review \u2192 address-confirmation \u2192 order placed \u2014 and the two\n      confirmation screenshots. Every finding names the heuristic it breaks, a severity, and the change\n      made in this prototype. Findings are ordered by severity within each screen.\n    </p>\n\n    <div class=\"row-end\" style=\"gap:var(--hb-space-24);margin-top:var(--hb-space-16);padding:var(--hb-space-16);background:var(--hb-color-surface);border:1px solid var(--hb-color-outline-variant);border-radius:var(--hb-radius-12)\">\n      <div><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span>Blocks or misleads on the path to purchase. Fix before release.</div>\n      <div><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span>Causes real friction or rework. High priority.</div>\n      <div><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span>Costs time or clarity. Low priority.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"metric\">\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">26</strong><span>findings</span></div>\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">6</strong><span>rated catastrophic</span></div>\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">10 / 10</strong><span>heuristics breached</span></div>\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">26</strong><span>addressed in this prototype</span></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Cart \u2014 <span class=\"num\">/storefront/cart</span></h2>\n    <table class=\"sheet\">\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Finding</th><th>Heuristic breached</th><th>Severity</th><th>Fix in this prototype</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C1</td>\n          <td>Quantity stays at <span class=\"num\">7</span> on an item flagged \"Only 1 item in stock\", and the line total still calculates as <span class=\"num\">BHD 7.000</span>.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Cart, Nadec Vanilla Flavored Milk 125ml.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">5 \u00b7 Error prevention</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">9 \u00b7 Recover from errors</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span></td>\n          <td>The line states the conflict, suppresses its total, and offers \"Reduce to 1\" plus a restock alert.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C2</td>\n          <td>Order Summary shows Subtotal <span class=\"num\">BHD 11.000</span> = Total <span class=\"num\">BHD 11.000</span>. A <span class=\"num\">BHD 10.000</span> delivery fee \u2014 <span class=\"num\">91%</span> of the basket \u2014 only appears on the next page.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Cart summary vs. review page.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span></td>\n          <td>Delivery, coupons and VAT are itemised in the cart summary. No figure changes between screens.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C3</td>\n          <td>A flat product grid, though minimum order, delivery fee, coupons and dispatch are all per supplier.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Cart shows five items with no supplier boundary; the review page then splits them.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">2 \u00b7 Match the real world</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">6 \u00b7 Recognition over recall</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>Items sit in supplier groups carrying that supplier's terms, subtotal and readiness.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C4</td>\n          <td>\"Minimum order for this product supplier: BHD 10.000. Add BHD 6.000 more or other items to proceed.\" repeated verbatim on every card in the group.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Four identical blocks in one viewport.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">8 \u00b7 Aesthetic and minimalist design</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>One progress bar per supplier: amount reached, target, exact gap, and a link that closes it.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C5</td>\n          <td>\"18pcs\" sits beside \"BHD 1.000\" with no per-piece figure, so comparing pack sizes is manual arithmetic.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Nadec Long Life Low Fat UHT Milk 200ml 18pcs.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">6 \u00b7 Recognition over recall</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">7 \u00b7 Flexibility and efficiency</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>Every line shows price per case, price per piece, and total pieces.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C6</td>\n          <td>One supplier below its minimum stalls the entire basket; the only routes out are buying more or deleting items.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Cart total drops from BHD 11.000 to BHD 4.000 as items are removed to get under way.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">3 \u00b7 User control and freedom</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>Ready suppliers check out now; the rest stays in the cart, named on the button's helper text.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C7</td>\n          <td>Deselecting items changes the header total silently, with no statement of what is included in the order.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">\"Select All\" and per-card checkboxes.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>The summary counts the lines it covers, and each supplier group states \"Ready to order\" or \"Excluded from this order\".</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>C8</td>\n          <td>No reorder, saved list or SKU entry anywhere in the flow.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">7 \u00b7 Flexibility and efficiency</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>Quick-add by SKU, \"Save as list\", and a recurring-basket prompt on the confirmation.</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Review \u2014 <span class=\"num\">/storefront/review</span></h2>\n    <table class=\"sheet\">\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Finding</th><th>Heuristic breached</th><th>Severity</th><th>Fix in this prototype</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>R1</td>\n          <td>\"Seller Total <span class=\"num\">BHD 10.000</span>\" appears after three discounts, with no order total beside it \u2014 it is unclear whether this is what will be charged.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Subtotal BHD 11.000, delivery BHD 10.000, three discounts, then \"Seller Total\".</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">4 \u00b7 Consistency and standards</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>One summary, one hierarchy: items \u2192 delivery \u2192 discounts \u2192 VAT \u2192 <b>Total</b>, identical on all three screens.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>R2</td>\n          <td>Discounts are labelled with raw internal codes \u2014 \"Mahmmod_Seller_code\", \"jpre\", \"10Dinar\" \u2014 that carry no meaning for the buyer.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">2 \u00b7 Match the real world</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>Each discount names its source and value: \"Coupon ALMANAR2 \u2014 supplier coupon, \u2212BHD 2.000\".</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>R3</td>\n          <td>The coupon entry field sits below the totals, at the bottom of the page, after the decision it affects.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">7 \u00b7 Flexibility and efficiency</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>Coupon entry sits at the top of the summary, above the figures it changes.</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Address &amp; documents \u2014 <span class=\"num\">/storefront/address-confirmation</span></h2>\n    <table class=\"sheet\">\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Finding</th><th>Heuristic breached</th><th>Severity</th><th>Fix in this prototype</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A1</td>\n          <td>The page carries no order summary and no total. The buyer presses \"Place Order\" with nothing on screen saying what is being bought or for how much.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Full page: verification header, branch details, address, documents, button.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span></td>\n          <td>A sticky summary with the full breakdown, present on every checkout screen.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A2</td>\n          <td>CR number, commercial licence and personal ID are uploaded inside the order \u2014 on every purchase, including repeat ones.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">7 \u00b7 Flexibility and efficiency</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">3 \u00b7 User control and freedom</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span></td>\n          <td>Verification moves to the account: checkout shows a verified chip with CR, VAT and expiry. Unverified buyers still order \u2014 dispatch waits, not the order.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A3</td>\n          <td>The uploaded ID renders full-bleed at its natural size, pushing \"Place Order\" thousands of pixels below the fold. A larger file pushes it further.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Screenshot 1: the image fills the viewport and continues past it.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">8 \u00b7 Aesthetic and minimalist design</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span></td>\n          <td>Attachments render as fixed-height rows \u2014 thumbnail, name, size, preview, remove. User content never sets page height.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A4</td>\n          <td>A panel labelled \"Step / Address &amp; Documents\" sits above the fold; a separate \"Step 2\" chip sits further down. Neither says how many steps exist.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">4 \u00b7 Consistency and standards</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>One indicator, three counted steps: Cart \u2192 Delivery &amp; purchase details \u2192 Payment.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A5</td>\n          <td>Field values are set in orange on white \u2014 <span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">Bahrain</span>, <span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">Manama</span>, <span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">18</span>, <span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">11111</span>. Measured contrast is <span class=\"num\">2.03:1</span>, and orange elsewhere in the interface means \"warning\", so settled values read as either links or problems.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">4 \u00b7 Consistency and standards</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>Values in near-black at <span class=\"num\">17.2:1</span>. Amber is reserved for genuine attention states; the whole palette is audited to <span class=\"num\">4.5:1</span> minimum.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A6</td>\n          <td>\"Place Order\" carries no amount, and no amount is visible anywhere on the page.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>\"Place order \u00b7 <span class=\"num\">BHD 11.000</span>\" on the button itself.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A7</td>\n          <td>No delivery date, time window or shipment count is offered or shown, though the order will split by supplier.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">2 \u00b7 Match the real world</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>Day and time-slot pickers per shipment, with capacity and the shipment count stated.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A8</td>\n          <td>No purchase order number, cost centre or invoice recipient \u2014 the fields a buyer's finance team reconciles against.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">2 \u00b7 Match the real world</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>Optional PO number, cost centre and invoice email, stated as printed on the tax invoice.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A9</td>\n          <td>\"Have VAT certificate\" is an unchecked box beside a large empty panel \u2014 roughly a third of the section is blank with no explanation of what checking it does.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Screenshot 1, Business Documents.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">8 \u00b7 Aesthetic and minimalist design</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">10 \u00b7 Help and documentation</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>VAT status is part of the account verification line, stated as a value rather than an empty container.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>A10</td>\n          <td>The map pin is required but never resolved back to anything \u2014 no confirmation of what address it corresponds to, and no way to tell a correct pin from a default one.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>The pin shows saved coordinates, is labelled as what drivers actually use, and is adjustable in place.</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Order placed \u2014 confirmation</h2>\n    <table class=\"sheet\">\n      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Finding</th><th>Heuristic breached</th><th>Severity</th><th>Fix in this prototype</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>P1</td>\n          <td>\"Click on Track Your Order to upload the transaction receipt\" \u2014 the page that creates the payment task sends the buyer elsewhere to complete it.\n            <span class=\"evidence\">Screenshot 4, below the bank details.</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">7 \u00b7 Flexibility and efficiency</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">10 \u00b7 Help and documentation</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"cancelled\"><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Catastrophic</span></td>\n          <td>The receipt dropzone sits directly under the bank details, with \"I'll pay later\" as the explicit alternative.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>P2</td>\n          <td>\"Your order has been placed successfully\" while payment is still outstanding \u2014 two contradictory states in one screen.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">4 \u00b7 Consistency and standards</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>\"Order received\", with the outstanding payment as the page's most prominent card and the current stage marked on a status timeline.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>P3</td>\n          <td>No payment deadline, no reservation window, no stated consequence of not transferring.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>A named expiry with a live countdown, and the stock-reservation rule stated in the first sentence.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>P4</td>\n          <td>No delivery date, no next steps, no route to the supplier. The page ends at the bank details.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">1 \u00b7 Visibility of system status</span><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">10 \u00b7 Help and documentation</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"pending\"><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 Major</span></td>\n          <td>A dated timeline through to invoicing, plus track, proforma download and message-supplier actions.</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>P5</td>\n          <td>The transfer reference is not stated, so a buyer paying from their bank app has no instruction on how the payment gets matched to the order.</td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-chip\" data-style=\"neutral\" data-size=\"sm\">10 \u00b7 Help and documentation</span></td>\n          <td><span class=\"hb-status\" data-status=\"approved\"><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Minor</span></td>\n          <td>Reference is a copyable field of its own, with the matching rule stated beneath it.</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Breaches by heuristic</h2>\n    <p>All ten heuristics are breached at least once, but the distribution is the finding: <b>visibility of\n      system status</b> accounts for <span class=\"num\">12</span> of the <span class=\"num\">38</span> breaches \u2014\n      nearly a third. The flow's characteristic failure is withholding cost, progress and state until after\n      the buyer has committed.</p>\n    <table class=\"tally\">\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">1</span> \u00b7 Visibility of system status</td><td class=\"num\">12</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">7</span> \u00b7 Flexibility and efficiency of use</td><td class=\"num\">5</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:42%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">2</span> \u00b7 Match between system and the real world</td><td class=\"num\">4</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:33%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">4</span> \u00b7 Consistency and standards</td><td class=\"num\">4</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:33%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">10</span> \u00b7 Help and documentation</td><td class=\"num\">4</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:33%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">8</span> \u00b7 Aesthetic and minimalist design</td><td class=\"num\">3</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:25%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">3</span> \u00b7 User control and freedom</td><td class=\"num\">2</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:17%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">6</span> \u00b7 Recognition rather than recall</td><td class=\"num\">2</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:17%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">5</span> \u00b7 Error prevention</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:8%\"></div></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><span class=\"num\">9</span> \u00b7 Recognise, diagnose and recover from errors</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:8%\"></div></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">What changed, in four numbers</h2>\n    <div class=\"metric\">\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">4 \u2192 3</strong><span>screens from cart to paid</span></div>\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">3 \u2192 0</strong><span>document uploads inside the order</span></div>\n      <div><strong>Screen <span class=\"num\">2</span> \u2192 <span class=\"num\">1</span></strong><span>where the delivery fee first appears</span></div>\n      <div><strong class=\"num\">2.03 \u2192 17.2</strong><span>contrast ratio on field values</span></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Principles behind the fixes</h2>\n    <div class=\"principles\">\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"padding:var(--hb-space-16)\"><h3 class=\"hb-title-md\">Total cost, from the first screen</h3><p>Delivery, VAT and discounts are visible in the cart and stay pinned through checkout. No number changes between screens.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"padding:var(--hb-space-16)\"><h3 class=\"hb-title-md\">The supplier is the unit</h3><p>Minimums, fees, coupons, dispatch and delivery windows all belong to a supplier group, and the cart is shaped that way.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"padding:var(--hb-space-16)\"><h3 class=\"hb-title-md\">Verify the buyer, not the order</h3><p>Trade documents live on the account and are collected once. Paperwork can delay dispatch; it can never block placing an order.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"padding:var(--hb-space-16)\"><h3 class=\"hb-title-md\">Repeat buying is the default</h3><p>SKU entry, saved lists and recurring baskets treat the second order as the main event, not the first.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"padding:var(--hb-space-16)\"><h3 class=\"hb-title-md\">Speaks procurement</h3><p>PO numbers, cost centres, reclaimable VAT, proforma invoices and Net 30 terms \u2014 the vocabulary a finance team already uses.</p></div>\n      <div class=\"panel\" style=\"padding:var(--hb-space-16)\"><h3 class=\"hb-title-md\">Legible and reachable</h3><p>4.5:1 minimum contrast, visible focus rings, real labels, tabular figures, keyboard-operable steppers, and full RTL support via logical properties.</p></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <h2 class=\"hb-headline-sm\">Method and limits</h2>\n    <p>\n      This is an expert inspection by a single evaluator, not a usability test \u2014 it predicts where buyers will\n      struggle, it does not measure that they do. Nielsen's own guidance is that one evaluator finds roughly a\n      third of the problems in an interface, so treat the count as a floor. Severity here weighs frequency,\n      impact and persistence, but no evaluator-agreement pass has been run, so ratings are one considered\n      opinion. The findings worth validating with real buyers first are <b>A2</b> (documents inside the order)\n      and <b>P1</b> (receipt upload on a separate page), because both trade against compliance and finance\n      constraints this evaluation cannot see.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n      Deliberately out of scope: catalogue and product pages, supplier onboarding, the credit-terms\n      application, returns, and the buyer's order-history area. Arabic copy in this prototype is\n      illustrative \u2014 the RTL toggle demonstrates layout mirroring, not final translation.\n    </p>\n  ";
